🚀 Azure Data Factory Project — Incremental Load for FactBookings1
📘 Overview
This project demonstrates an incremental data load pipeline built using Azure Data Factory (ADF).
It integrates data from an Azure SQL Database into Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2, ensuring efficient, scalable, and monitored data movement.

The pipeline automates:

🔍 Lookup of previous and latest load timestamps

⚙️ Conditional data extraction from SQL

📤 Copying incremental data into Data Lake

🧩 Updating watermark values for future runs

🧩 Repository Structure
File	Description
Additional_Data_Insert.docx	Contains SQL INSERT statements for new records in the FactBookings1 table. Used for testing incremental load logic.
Load_FactBookings1.csv	Sample dataset representing bookings data to be loaded into the SQL table. Used for initial or full-load scenarios.
README.md	Documentation for setup, configuration, and pipeline execution.


🏗️ Pipeline Components
1️⃣ Lookup Activities
lastload_FactBookings1 → Retrieves the last successful load timestamp from Data Lake.

latestload → Fetches the latest available data timestamp from SQL.

2️⃣ Copy Data Activities
Copy_data_FactBookings1 → Copies incremental data from SQL to Data Lake based on lookup results.

WaterMark → Updates the watermark file (lastload) after successful copy.

📂 Data Flow
text
Azure SQL Database (Source)
        ↓
